; Provider-route executable family, 7 of 7 — the per-source name
; ceiling, tripped end-to-end.
;
; `ProviderExtraction.MAX_EXTRACTED_NAMES` is 4096, and unlike most of
; SJON's ceilings it is trivially reachable: a provider is a program, and
; a program can return 4097 names as easily as two. So it takes a direct
; trip case rather than a runtime seam, and 4097 is spelled here because
; a corpus fixture cannot import a Zig constant.
;
; Over the cap the whole extraction is a failure — not a truncation. A
; silently truncated member set would make `not_cross_ref` depend on
; where a name happened to sit in the provider's output, which is the
; kind of answer that differs between hosts for no reason a user could
; ever discover. So it takes the same poisoned-bucket path a refusal
; does: one diagnostic, and `n0` below goes unchecked despite being a
; name the provider would certainly have emitted.
(use-plugin "lines")

(counter :name c :src "4097")

(use :n n0)
